"We now have a working CLI that downloads the artifacts, and a prototype web that reads the artifacts and display the content. Now let's make them enterprise level. For the CLI, it should not just read from a folder on the airgap side, it should also inject the data into the enterprise modelhub. We have Artifactory with limited hfapi installed, you can refer to the specs here https://docs.jfrog.com/artifactory/docs/use-hugging-face-with-jfrog-cli. meta data should also be installed in a database. Now, based on the artifacts we will use, design an architecture to host all the artifacts, metadata, models and whatever we downloaded using CLI. The architecture should be hosted via docker containers."
